    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To both parties. The deviation itself is real and is measured on this trip's own instruments: the GPS trace on EV-GPS-00520 runs 5.63 km between the recorded pickup and dropoff against the booked optimal of 3.1 km on EV-TRIP-00520, an excess of 2.53 km, or 81.6%, which passes both POL-RD-01 establishment limbs (over 20% and over 0.8 km) and crosses the 50% materiality gate. But the driver is not at fault for it. The in-app chat (EV-CHAT-00520) records the rider asking at 11:37:10, one minute after the 11:36:40 start and well inside POL-RD-04's three-minute window, 'can stop at Sheng Siong Blk 501 first? need to grab something', carrying a platform-resolved waypoint_hint (Sheng Siong Supermarket, Blk 501 Tampines Central 1), and the rider confirms it in her own statement: 'I did ask him to stop at the supermarket, that is true.' POL-RD-04 therefore exonerates the excess. The rider's argument for a SGD 3.95 partial refund under POL-RD-02 is rejected: POL-RD-02 runs only where a deviation is established and no exculpatory clause fully excuses it, and POL-RD-04 fully excuses this one, the whole 2.53 km being the requested supermarket stop with no other cause of excess in evidence. The rider's further point, that POL-RD-04 excludes excess distance but not excess time, does not survive either: POL-RD-02 is triggered by a POL-RD-01 distance deviation, and once that deviation is exonerated the recomputation does not run, so the time line as billed stands. What the record does show is that the driver was paid for only the booked 3.1 km while the trace records 5.63 km - a shortfall of 2.53 unbilled kilometres, past POL-RD-04's 1.0 km gate. That clause pays SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre: 2.53 x 0.75 = SGD 1.8975, rounded UP to the nearest 0.05 = SGD 1.90, far under the SGD 15.00 per-trip cap. The outcome is DRIVER_COMPENSATION, and the amount the ruling moves is SGD 1.90, which is also the figure in driver_compensation_sgd; the rider's own charge is not refunded, and under POL-GEN-03 the driver payment is not netted against any rider refund. On the remaining points: the missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00520-01 (status MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) can carry no fact, so no POL-RD-03 traffic exoneration exists and none is needed, because the driver relies on the rider's instruction and not on an external traffic cause - the absence neither cuts the excess nor engages POL-RD-10(5). No POL-RD-10 escalation fires: trip identifiers match across EV-TRIP-00520, EV-GPS-00520 and EV-FARE-00520; the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) with 121 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage and no gaps; no timestamps disagree; the amount is far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling and below charged_total 12.53; and every charge line (base fare 3.80, distance 2.33, time 5.60, platform fee 0.80, zero ERP) has its counterpart in the trip record, so no billing-integrity referral arises under POL-RD-09(4). The driver_profile check comes back clean - deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 250, below both POL-RD-06 tests - so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral.",
    "amount_note": null
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 1.9,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 1.9,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To both parties — here is what the evidence decides.\n\n1. The detour is established, but it was the rider's own request. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00520, weight 1.0) records 5.63 km driven between the recorded pickup and dropoff; the booked optimal route (EV-TRIP-00520) is 3.1 km. The excess is 2.53 km, or 81.6% over optimal — over both POL-RD-01 thresholds (20% and 0.8 km) and over the 50% material gate. But POL-RD-04 exonerates an excess caused by a rider instruction recorded in the chat log. At 11:37:10, about one minute into the trip, the rider wrote in the in-app chat (EV-CHAT-00520): 'can stop at Sheng Siong Blk 501 first? need to grab something', carrying the platform-resolved waypoint (1.3549, 103.9458) for Sheng Siong Blk 501 Tampines Central 1; the driver replied 'ok'. The rider's own statement confirms this: 'I did ask him to stop at the supermarket, that is true.' The instruction came from the rider, was sent well inside the three-minute window POL-RD-04(b) allows, and names a place specific enough to act on, with a non-null waypoint_hint — so the clause's corroboration test is runnable and is satisfied. The whole 2.53 km excess is attributable to that requested stop; nothing else on the record accounts for the extra distance. The excess is therefore excluded before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 run, no deviation remains, and no distance-or-time refund arises. In any event the rider was billed only 3.1 km on the distance line (EV-FARE-00520), so she never paid for the detour distance.\n\n2. The driver is owed the unbilled distance. The fare billed 3.1 km while the trace records 5.63 km — an unbilled shortfall of 2.53 km, over POL-RD-04's 1.0 km gate. At the policy rate of SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre, 2.53 x 0.75 = 1.8975, rounded UP to the nearest SGD 0.05, giving SGD 1.90 — the exact sum the driver contested, and far under the SGD 15.00 per-trip cap. Under POL-GEN-03 this is a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling: amount_sgd carries the same SGD 1.90 as driver_compensation_sgd. It is a payment to the driver, it is NOT netted against the rider's fare, and the rider's charge stands as billed (NO_ACTION on the charge).\n\n3. Checks run. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (121 fixes, 10-second cadence, coverage 100%, empty gaps array, max inter-fix gap 0 s, no jump over 500 m, no interval over 30 s), so POL-RD-10(3) does not apply and the finding may rest on the trace. No traffic advisory is on file: EV-ADVIS-00520-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and no closure exoneration is available — the driver invokes none and does not need one. Because the deviation is material, POL-RD-06 required the driver-profile check: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 250, below both pattern tests, so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: trip identifiers match across EV-TRIP-00520, EV-GPS-00520 and EV-FARE-00520, the timestamps agree and do not run backwards, the refund ceiling is not approached, and every charge line (base 3.80, distance 2.33, time 5.60, platform fee 0.80, zero ERP) has its counterpart. No clause produces a referral, so the referrals list is empty.\n\n4. Claims answered. The rider's argument that the detour cannot be quantified, and her separate argument that POL-RD-04 has no duration limb so the time charge survives, are rejected: the record quantifies the total excess (2.53 km); the rider's request with its resolved waypoint, her admission that she asked for the stop, and the trace's otherwise-unexplained excess together attribute the whole of it; and with the excess fully excluded no deviation is established and POL-RD-02 does not run. The rider's points that the trace is unimpaired and that the missing advisory removes any POL-RD-03 exoneration are accepted, but they do not change the outcome. The driver's POL-RD-06 point (no pattern) is accepted; his POL-RD-04 exoneration and compensation claims are accepted and are the basis of this ruling."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

