    "explanation": "Both parties agree on the fact that decides this case, so it can be ruled on rather than sent to a human. [Rider], your in-app message at 11:37:10 on EV-CHAT-00520 — 'can stop at Sheng Siong Blk 501 first?' — carries the platform-resolved waypoint (Sheng Siong Supermarket, Blk 501 Tampines Central 1), and your own statement ('I did ask him to stop at the supermarket, that is true') confirms it. That is a rider instruction that is specific enough to act on and was sent inside the first minute of the trip, well within POL-RD-04's 3-minute window, and the trace (121 fixes, 10 s cadence, no gaps, 5.63 km driven) is consistent with a genuinely longer drive. The extra distance is therefore rider-caused and is excluded before the deviation and fare-recomputation clauses run.\n\n[Driver], that exclusion cuts both ways. It means the fare you billed stands, but it also means the same clause's compensation limb applies to you: EV-FARE-00520 shows the rider was billed distance_charged_km 3.1 (the booked optimal), while EV-GPS-00520 records trace_distance_km 5.63 — an unbilled shortfall of 2.53 km, past the 1.0 km gate. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre, 2.53 x 0.75 = SGD 1.8975, rounded up to SGD 1.90, far under the SGD 15.00 per-trip cap. That is the sum you contested and it is granted as DRIVER_COMPENSATION. Per POL-GEN-03, amount_sgd carries the same SGD 1.90; this is a platform-side payment for unbilled distance, not a second charge to the rider, whose SGD 12.53 charge stands.\n\n[Rider]'s request for a distance/time refund is declined. Her advocate asked for the POL-RD-02 recomputation (charged_total SGD 12.53 less recomputed_fare SGD 8.605 = SGD 3.925, i.e. SGD 3.95), and the arithmetic is correct, but POL-RD-04 removes the rider-caused excess from the deviation before POL-RD-01 and POL-RD-02 are applied, so that recomputation does not run and no part of the fare is returned.\n\nFigures used: charged_total SGD 12.53; booked optimal distance 3.1 km; trace distance 5.63 km; unbilled distance 2.53 km; rate SGD 0.75/km; compensation SGD 1.90. No traffic advisory covers this trip (EV-ADVIS-00520-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), so no external-cause exoneration was available — but neither party relied on a traffic cause, so it changes nothing. The trace is unimpaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (no gap over 90 s, no 500 m jump, no sampling interval over 30 s), and no POL-RD-10 trigger fires. No repeat-deviation pattern exists (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d 0 over 250 trips), so there is no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral, and with no ERP gantries or airport surcharge there is no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral. All artifacts carrying the deciding facts — the chat log, the trip record, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown — are at weight_multiplier 1.0, so confidence is 0.90.",
